  "summary": "Session 6 of Murphy's lucid-dreaming series: after five weekly temporal sessions, the same amygdala and hippocampal signals in sequence over the frontal lobes. Murphy reports cases of lucid dreaming 'that very night'.",
  "setting": "Run it on the night you want to dream; end it 1 to 1.5 h before going to bed. Dark, quiet room, eyes closed.",
  "schedule": "Once, a week after session 5 of murphy-shakti-lucid-dream-series-temporal; then the vendor's 21-day break. Murphy says effective temporal sessions are 'probably ... a prerequisite', so do not start the series with this file.",
  "notes": "30 min on four frontal coils, Fp1 and AF3 on the left, Fp2 and AF4 on the right (the vendor shows the frontal placement only in photos, so these sites are an inference); the other four channels stay silent. All four play the same signal together. Both signals are proprietary. The amygdala 'burstx' template is approximated by the built-in accelerating burst (6 to 30 Hz over 230 points, the point count of the published burst-firing pattern, drawn on the Shakti's 3-ms points = 0.69 s), the hippocampal 'LTP' template by 4 bursts of 4 biphasic pulses 9 ms apart repeated at 5.4 Hz (the vendor's reported LTP spectral peak), also on 3-ms points. As the vendor describes, the two follow each other with a 4-s silence after each: amygdala 0.69 s, silence 4 s, hippocampus 0.74 s, silence 4 s (a 9.4-s cycle). Murphy notes that 'There have not been many reports' of lucid dreams after the series, so do not expect it to produce them. The vendor reports headache or pressure in about 2% of users with hippocampal signals; if so, lower the intensity by one third. Not for people with epilepsy or a seizure history; stop at once on fear or any distress. Independent double-blind tests found no effect of God-Helmet-type fields (Granqvist 2005; Gendle & McGrath 2012).",
  "targets": ["left-dlpfc", "right-dlpfc", "vmpfc"],
